# The loop of merge-descriptors. The names are worked out, so no statement lays `size` or `first` on the prototype object by name, and nothing is proven of what stands there.
# Link expects under each name what the field of the literal holds (link/members-that-a-loop-copies-off-a-literal-are-expected-on-the-prototype-object.ir), the record of the class lists both, and each call in the loop asks the guard of its name and goes to the one function.
# f1 = Bag, f2 = mixin, f3 = run, f4 = size, f5 = first, L0 = Bag
# RUN(SIZE): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# SIZE: {layout=L0 key="size"}
# RUN(FIRST): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# FIRST: {layout=L0 key="first"}
# RUN(COPIED): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# COPIED: frame {{*}} callee=f4
# COPIED: frame {{*}} callee=f5
# RUN(CALLED): walk f3 mechanisms=all-Inlining
# CALLED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f4
# CALLED: = CallDirect {{*}} function=f5
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell
# ANSWER: 50
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(APART): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Inlining
# APART: 50
# APART-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CLOSED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all-Guesses
